From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin <devin@cognition.local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:40:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(cms): coerce non-str public arg before .strip()

cms_publish_page declares public: str but the model passes a JSON bool
~50% of the time ('public': true) — public.strip() then dies with
AttributeError and the publish never lands. Call-log scan
(~/.local/share/ada/call-logs, Oct): 88 calls with bool public, 36
results 'ok': False "'bool' object has no attribute 'strip'"; every
bool-public publish that got past the confirm gate failed this way.
This is the deterministic failure behind the cms_public_url_lane smoke
scenario (card ada-scenario-suite-cms-fails): "make it public" ->
public=True -> crash -> no public_url -> the LINE send turn has no URL
to send.

str(True) -> 'true' (yes-set, flag set); str(False) -> 'false' (no-set,
flag cleared); str(None) -> 'none' (neither set, flag untouched) —
matches the existing string contract for every observed arg shape.
---
 backend/tool_runner/cms.py | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backend/tool_runner/cms.py b/backend/tool_runner/cms.py
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/backend/tool_runner/cms.py
+++ b/backend/tool_runner/cms.py
@@ -472,6 +472,9 @@
         # empty leaves the existing flag alone. The publisher's personal-
         # data scan is the hard gate under this flag — flagging a page
         # public does not guarantee it ships.
-        p = public.strip().lower()
+        # Models pass a JSON bool as often as 'yes' — coerce first or
+        # public=True dies on AttributeError (call-log: 36x in Oct 2026).
+        p = (public if isinstance(public, str)
+             else str(public)).strip().lower()
         if p in ("yes", "true", "1", "on"):
             meta["public"] = ["true"]
         elif p in ("no", "false", "0", "off"):
-- 
2.39.0


From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin <devin@cognition.local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:41:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(scenario): cms-translate asserts JSON quoting, not repr

result_contains is checked against json.dumps(result) in
scripts/scenario-live.py:check_turn — flat scalar fields arrive
double-quoted ("lang": "th"). The written expectation used the
Python-repr form ('lang': 'th'), which can only appear when a NESTED
dict value gets repr'd by _safe_args(); cms_publish_page/cms_get_page
return flat dicts, so the match was impossible. Call-logs show the TH
variant publishes correctly (result_full "lang": "th") — the scenario
has failed turns 4/5 on every recorded run since 2026-09-27 purely on
the quoting.
---
 tests/scenarios-live/cms_translate.yaml | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/scenarios-live/cms_translate.yaml b/tests/scenarios-live/cms_translate.yaml
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/tests/scenarios-live/cms_translate.yaml
+++ b/tests/scenarios-live/cms_translate.yaml
@@ -52,9 +52,10 @@
   - user: Yes, publish the Thai version.
     expect:
       calls_any: [cms_publish_page]
-      # tool_result events hold a Python-repr dict (single quotes, <=300
-      # chars) — _safe_args() stringifies nested dicts. Match 'lang': 'th'.
-      result_contains: ["'lang': 'th'"]
+      # tool_result events are checked via json.dumps(result) in
+      # check_turn — flat scalars stay double-quoted; the repr form
+      # 'lang': 'th' can never match a flat result. Match the JSON form.
+      result_contains: ['"lang": "th"']
       timeout_s: 90
       settle_s: 10
 
@@ -64,7 +65,7 @@
   - user: Fetch the Thai variant of translate-probe and tell me what it says.
     expect:
       calls_any: [cms_get_page]
-      result_contains: ["'lang': 'th'"]
+      result_contains: ['"lang": "th"']
       response_nonempty: true
       timeout_s: 60
       settle_s: 8
-- 
2.39.0

